            },
            {
              "type": "header",
              "txt": "Intranet"
            },
            {
              "type": "content",
              "txt": "Log onto Bagwan Health's Interpreting services intranet home page"
            },
            {
              "type": "row",
              "buttons": [
                {
                  "txt": "Go to laboratory intranet home page",
                  "uri": "/Bagwan2.0/scorm/department-pages/lab-technologies/index.html"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "rotateX": "-12",
          "rotateY": "-150"
        },
        {
          "card": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/hotspot_images/Pathology_computer.jpg"
            },
            {
              "type": "header",
              "txt": "Welcome to the laboratory"
            },
            {
              "type": "content",
              "txt": "Specimen reception is responsible for the initial stage of sample processing and laboratory. Samples are received from a variety of sources, including JPS, wards and outpatients in the hospital.\n\nSome samples may be urgent, which needs to be identified and prioritised to get those urgent requests to the relevant disciplines immediately.\n\nSamples types that can be received are blood, urine, sputum, swabs and faeces.\n\nThe disciplines that we have here are biochemistry, haematology, blood transfusion and microbiology."
            },
            {
              "type": "row",
              "buttons": []
            }
          ],
          "rotateX": "0",
          "rotateY": "0"
        },
        {
          "card": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/hotspot_images/Pathology_test.jpg"
            },
            {
              "type": "header",
              "txt": "Handling and processing specimens"
            },
            {
              "type": "content",
              "txt": "Lab requisition\nMust be filled out correctly\nReview to ensure all information is correct\nVerify test, time and date of collection\nPatient information\nDoctor information\nTest request\n\n\nHandling of specimens\nAvoid unnecessary shaking and agitation to sample\nAvoid spillage\nStopper place facing upwards\nInvert immediately\nSecure lids\nWear gloves\n"
            },
            {
              "type": "row",
              "buttons": []
            }
          ],
          "rotateX": "-9",
          "rotateY": "45"
        },
        {
          "card": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/hotspot_images/HazardousWaste.jpg"
            },
            {
              "type": "header",
              "txt": "Handling and disposal of waste materials"
            },
            {
              "type": "content",
              "txt": "Proper hazardous waste management can prevent the risk of spreading infectious diseases as well as prevent the risk of needlestick injuries.\n\nClick the link below to test your knowledge on handling and disposal of waste materials in the laboratory. "
            },
            {
              "type": "row",
              "buttons": [
                {
                  "txt": "Test your knowledge on hazardous waste management",
                  "uri": "/Bagwan2.0/scorm/department-pages/lab-technologies/waste-management/index.html"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "rotateX": "-30",
          "rotateY": "95"
        },
        {
          "card": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/hotspot_images/handwashing.jpg"
            },
            {
              "type": "header",
              "txt": "Hand washing procedure"
            },
            {
              "type": "content",
              "txt": "Hand hygiene is key to the prevention of infections and the transmission of antimicrobial resistance. The World Health Organisation has provided this guideline on health hygiene in health care. "
            },
            {
              "type": "row",
              "buttons": [
                {
                  "txt": "Download the WHO orgnanisation hand hygiene guide",
                  "uri": "http://whqlibdoc.who.int/publications/2009/9789241597906_eng.pdf?ua=1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "rotateX": "-5",
          "rotateY": "130"
        },
        {
          "card": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/hotspot_images/EmergencyShower.png"
            },
            {
              "type": "header",
              "txt": "Emergency shower procedure"
            },
            {
              "type": "content",
              "txt": "An emergency eyewash and safety shower should be available in every laboratory that uses chemicals and hazardous substances. Emergency showers can also be used effectively in extinguishing clothing fires or for flushing contaminants off clothing."
            },
            {
              "type": "row",
              "buttons": []
            }
          ],
          "rotateX": "-5",
          "rotateY": "145"
        }
